<title>USA: Woolworth CEO sees closings as cash flow neutral.</title>
<headline>Woolworth CEO sees closings as cash flow neutral.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woolworth Corp chairman and chief executive Roger Farah said the company's decision to close all 400 of its U.S. five and dime stores should be cash flow neutral to positive in two years.</p>
<p>The company is aiming to make its cash flow positive in less than two years through the planned conversion of about 100 of its locations into sporting goods and athletic footwear formats, Farah said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Woolworth currently owns 3,600 sporting goods and athletic footwear stores under the Champs Sports and Foot Locker names.</p>
</text>
